{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew","id":1291469,"title":"Potentially politically problematic homebrew?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-24T02:36:20-08:00","id":1291469,"title":"Potentially politically problematic homebrew?","content":"Ok, um.... <br /> <br /> Alright. Fine. I'm planning on writing several demons. They may be politically incorrect, or uncomfortable. Mind if you review them for me? <br /> <br /> 1. A demon that can copy or imitate any ethnicity. Its purpose is to instigate strife and disunity amongst Creation's peoples. Basically, a terrorist. Random stabbings. Arson. Sabotage. Firedust explosives. Poisonings. Absurdly good at guerilla warfare, improvised weaponry and traps, inciting hate and fear, and has a larceny specialty in setting up incriminating evidence and false rumours<br /> 2. A spell that summons a construct, or a first circle demon. A predator drone, basically. Good eyesight, good senses, and ranged weaponry that hits from miles. Roll a limit whenever it sees celebrations and joyous occasions, and doesn't attack it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T02:52:53-08:00","id":1291472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew#post1291469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, um....<br /> <br /> Alright. Fine. I'm planning on writing several demons. They may be politically incorrect, or uncomfortable. Mind if you review them for me?<br /> <br /> 1. A demon that can copy or imitate any ethnicity. Its purpose is to instigate strife and disunity amongst Creation's peoples. Basically, a terrorist. Random stabbings. Arson. Sabotage. Firedust explosives. Poisonings. Absurdly good at guerilla warfare, improvised weaponry and traps, inciting hate and fear, and has a larceny specialty in setting up incriminating evidence and false rumours<br /> 2. A spell that summons a construct, or a first circle demon. A predator drone, basically. Good eyesight, good senses, and ranged weaponry that hits from miles. Roll a limit whenever it sees celebrations and joyous occasions, and doesn't attack it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lets work backwards. <br /> <br /> 2--A misery seeking Agatae that has a ranged weapon is functionally fine. In fact, unless called out in someway as &quot;this is a predator drone&quot;, it is likely to go unnoticed. I'm not sure people noticed that I put 3 XKCD references and 2 HS references in my demon book, for Jebus sake.<br /> <br /> 1. Here we have to disect somethings. I guess the start is, what is the goal of the demon?<br /> A demon designed to sow racial tensions in creation is trick. I'm going to temporarily sidestep the &quot;but would Creation even have those sorts of racial tensions without a European Colonial Power invested in generating them for it's own benefit/The REalm is a colonial empire and thus assuredly has some degree of racial structraling built in&quot; point and say simply that &quot;sow disunity by means of race&quot; is a fairly limiting practice. I think a demon who's schtick is they can copy someone's appearance....runs face first into the ardent jaws of a Lunar. Making a non-lunar shapeshifter is ALSO possible, but generally it's by limiting their shape in some way. <br /> The powers also seem a bit split. Again, ignoring the bit in Compass : Malfeas where there are Blood Ape Supremacists, if the goal is &quot;incite hate crimes against other mortals&quot; gueriall warfare is unneccessary. You have mortals for that! You want rumor mongering and larceny. As written, the demon is both instigator and actor--I'd maybe focus on one more than the other.<br /> <br /> Now lets come back down to &quot;is this a good idea&quot;. The answer is...not terribly. A demon meant to sow discord fits into the Yozi's standard operating procedure. However, I think this version is grounded in imitating modern problems that are not as prevalent during the Bronze Age. I'd suggest re-examining the goal of the demon, and considering what bizzare or alien ways it could approach that goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:15:22-08:00","id":1291477,"title":"","content":"Main driver should be: Will this upset anyone in your group and mess with your dynamic? You're not harming anyone off your table by writing these things after all.<br /> <br /> For the shapeshifting demon, I don't think demons that sow and feed on hatred and conflict are off limits, whether you want to have them work through this sort of &quot;Pretend to be a bad Samaritan then commit terror&quot; or not, sort of idea, or more like sowing stories, manipulating and co-opting people into wicked acts, etc.<br /> <br /> The only caution I would suggest is that this would seem to be giving a pretty wide ranging shapeshifting/disguise power to a First Circle(?) demon that can be summoned and bound by player characters and by setting NPCs, and you might want to think carefully through consequences for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:28:04-08:00","id":1291479,"title":"","content":"Alright, then. How about this? Remember all those rumour mongering that Kings did to Jews, so they didn't need to pay them debts? Remember the tales of sacrifice and cannibalism that religions tell of each other? <br /> <br /> How about... Not just ethnicities, but everything. The demon not only can copy appearance, but with a charm, can make it so that anyone that perceives him knows immediately what he is. Is he christian? Wiccan? Muslim? Worshipper of Ahlat? Worshipper of the Mammoth god? A member of the police? A worshipper of Dreaming Spice, goddess of cocaine? <br /> <br /> I'm trying to think about racia riots, the historical oppression of immigrants to the United States, and religious progroms and purges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T03:33:59-08:00","id":1291481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1291477#post1291477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Main driver should be: Will this upset anyone in your group and mess with your dynamic? You're not harming anyone off your table by writing these things after all.<br /> <br /> For the shapeshifting demon, I don't think demons that sow and feed on hatred and conflict are off limits, whether you want to have them work through this sort of &quot;Pretend to be a bad Samaritan then commit terror&quot; or not, sort of idea, or more like sowing stories, manipulating and co-opting people into wicked acts, etc.<br /> <br /> The only caution I would suggest is that this would seem to be giving a pretty wide ranging shapeshifting/disguise power to a First Circle(?) demon that can be summoned and bound by player characters and by setting NPCs, and you might want to think carefully through consequences for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, there are no players. <br /> <br /> Just lonely me, writing a demon. <br /> <br /> The shapeshifting part works, too. Perhaps a drawback?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:06:48-08:00","id":1291489,"title":"","content":"It seems a bit unnecessary tbh, you dont need any kind of magic to place blame on a particular social group, just scrawl a provocative message next to your crime scene and your pretty much done, i dont think you need a demon to specialize in doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T04:25:17-08:00","id":1291493,"title":"","content":"Ranged weaponry with a range of literal miles strikes me as OP. I'd look at existing range-extending Charms for a benchmark on what is possible here. The fact that it's basically a predator drone is only a problem if you think someone at your table will have a problem with it. <br /> <br /> I don't see anything inherently wrong with the concept of &quot;shapeshifting trickster demon that sows discord by posing as a human identifiable as belonging to a particular group and then committing crimes&quot; but for godssake, don't make its default form reminiscent of any real-world groups associated in the public imagination with terrorism.<br /> <br /> I'd also add that if you really plan to make racism a central theme in any story then at least do some cursory research into the structural dimensions of racism and racial violence because shit be complicated and you don't want to cartoonify a sensitive issue. The same goes for terrorism and radicalisation if you want to explore those themes. It's not that any of this can't be done well, it's just that you have to know your stuff or you'll be opening a can of worms with more teeth than you expected.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T06:43:12-08:00","id":1291515,"title":"","content":"The concept of a demon that loves to cause strife and chaos, frame people for crimes, etc, is fine. Though it should be done in a sufficiently weird way, being a demon.<br /> <br /> Maybe it impersonates people, then carries out distinctly weird crimes that a demonologist would recognise. Cutting out the eyes of monks. Strangling professional singers. Etc.<br /> <br /> But &quot;it can change ethnicity&quot; seems a)too human, not demonic, and b)not something that would be as effective in most of Creation that it would be in the modern USA, which you are considering.<br /> <br /> The USA's social tensions are not the most racialised of any society ever, of course. But they are more-so than most societies, past or present.<br /> <br /> If you're in Arjuf, and start stabbing people as a dark-skinned guy, that's not going to make people think &quot;black people are dangerous!&quot; Because they don't categorise people into black and white (because, frankly, it's actually a weird way to categorise people for various complex reasons. I really don't understand why Americans have one category for people of Spanish descent, and another for every other European ethnicity). They categorise people by social caste and whether they are from the Realm or not. But 6000 years as the centre of Creation means that while a lot of people look like, essentially, tall Chinese people, there's plenty of people with all kinds of different features.<br /> <br /> And then of course, if you go to a peasant village in the far reaches of the Threshold... pretty much everyone's going to have the same ethnic features anyway. No-one in the deep South is going to have green or blue hair, it's all going to be black, dark brown, or red.<br /> <br /> There are places where this will work of course. Places with poorly-assimilated different ethnic groups, whose cultural identity is bound up in racial features*. Varang, with its Djala slaves. Greyfalls, with distinct-looking tribes (like, one is blue and has 6 fingers) who have different economic and political roles.<br /> <br /> *It's important to remember how similar many ethnic groups actually look. Like, if a Scottish person went on a rampage through my town, I could identify them as Scottish by their speech, but not by looks, because they look pretty similar to we English. Honestly, I probably couldn't even identify a killer as a Russian, or an Italian. If I see a big group of French people, I can tell, but not an individual. Similarly, I can tell a group of Koreans from a group of Japanese or a group of Chinese, but not individuals. Most Chinese people I knew thought my Japanese neighbour was Chinese until they heard him speaking. I've been mistaken as a Jew, a Pakistani, and a Turk twice (once by a Turkish guy). Identifying people's ethnic groups is not easy. That's why Americans use such ludicrously big categories as &quot;White&quot; and &quot;Black&quot;, and even those are sometimes difficult to identify. It's also why a lot of ethnic groups use distinct clothing, jewelry or hair styles to identify themselves, because skin colour and face shape isn't good enough.<br /> <br /> So, maybe it'd be better to have a demon who's obsessed with, say, heraldry and clothes? Like they wrap themselves in a cloak with the symbols of House Ragara, when they go on their mad killing spree. Or they dress up in Ishvanti clothes when murdering people across Harborhead, and this makes people turn on the Ishvanti. Or they dress up as an Immaculate Monk while killing in Chiaroscoro, which makes people turn on the Realm. Or, similarly, they wear a Delzahn veil and people turn on the Tri-Khan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T18:44:47-08:00","id":1291678,"title":"","content":"That's a wonderful idea. Maybe I can get inspiration from the Iz","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T02:57:46-08:00","id":1291760,"title":"","content":"Maybe the predator drone demon's attack is like a bee's sting? A one-time weapon that's ultimately used at the cost of their life.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T03:28:53-08:00","id":1291770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1291760#post1291760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the predator drone demon's attack is like a bee's sting? A one-time weapon that's ultimately used at the cost of their life.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Two attacks? One suicide launch, another one that lets it carry out harassment? I'm thinking of a massive metamorphosis into a missile for the first, and mouths that spit out death threats for the second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T20:22:43-08:00","id":1292350,"title":"","content":"Your demon sounds a lot like a tulpa or doppelganger, further empowered by a set of specialized Charms for sowing discord. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T00:20:51-08:00","id":1292399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292350#post1292350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your demon sounds a lot like a tulpa or doppelganger, further empowered by a set of specialized Charms for sowing discord.</div> </div> </div> </div> It is. Meant for mischief and spreading chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T00:21:44-08:00","id":1292400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292350#post1292350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your demon sounds a lot like a tulpa or doppelganger, further empowered by a set of specialized Charms for sowing discord.</div> </div> </div> </div> It is. Meant for mischief and spreading chaos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T11:03:33-08:00","id":1292536,"title":"","content":"You could refer to Twin Peaks for some ideas. Though they would be more creepy/horror themes than epic fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T04:44:14-08:00","id":1292730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew#post1291469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, um....<br /> <br /> Alright. Fine. I'm planning on writing several demons. They may be politically incorrect, or uncomfortable. Mind if you review them for me?<br /> <br /> 1. A demon that can copy or imitate any ethnicity. Its purpose is to instigate strife and disunity amongst Creation's peoples. Basically, a terrorist. Random stabbings. Arson. Sabotage. Firedust explosives. Poisonings. Absurdly good at guerilla warfare, improvised weaponry and traps, inciting hate and fear, and has a larceny specialty in setting up incriminating evidence and false rumours<br /> 2. A spell that summons a construct, or a first circle demon. A predator drone, basically. Good eyesight, good senses, and ranged weaponry that hits from miles. Roll a limit whenever it sees celebrations and joyous occasions, and doesn't attack it.</div> </div> </div> </div>N1 feels limited. Faking ethnicity might be enough to disguise as part of a populace, but that's about it. Neomah can do better sans for the demonic presence. But Neomah's a good baseline for you.<br /> N2 feels similarly limited. Demon Summoning already does just that, if that's what you want it to do. A creature that &quot;can attack from miles away&quot; will be a big deal, as that's a big deal even for the exalted. It might be off the table for First Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T04:49:28-08:00","id":1292731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1291472#post1291472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A demon designed to sow racial tensions in creation is trick. I'm going to temporarily sidestep the &quot;but would Creation even have those sorts of racial tensions without a European Colonial Power invested in generating them for it's own benefit/The REalm is a colonial empire and thus assuredly has some degree of racial structraling built in&quot; point and say simply that &quot;sow disunity by means of race&quot; is a fairly limiting practice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer is yes, though. &quot;Being wary of the other&quot; is a very, very basal reaction humans have (and most anything else, really). Racism derivates from that quite easily.<br /> <br /> If &quot;heredity&quot; is a thing, any given people that managed to exist mostly uniformly will form a mostly uniform ethnicity. This is especially true of people with geographic barriers, like the whole of Creation.<br /> And heredity is a thing in Creation.<br /> So most populaces will be relatively uniform. And being surprised or wary of something different, or assuming better off the similar, will happen. The steps for that to become what we usually understand as racism are short and natural.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 02-28-2019, 07:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T07:39:19-08:00","id":1292759,"title":"","content":"Yeah the attack from miles away range is a tough one. Even in the real world with all of our advanced technology there are a lot of forces that don\u2019t have any way to protect against a predator drone. Even if it\u2019s a one shot only deal the attack could be a problem, especially if it can fly at high altitude.<br /> <br /> What you could maybe do is have it launch it\u2019s one missile that travels at high speed, but not actual missile speed, to its target. Then after it strikes the ground it builds up charge my sucking energy from the dragon-lines until it explodes. That way super fast reacting exalts could maybe pick it out of the air on its way, and everyone else would have like 1-2 rounds to kill it before it blows up their whole gathering. It could be decently durable so it\u2019s not a guarantee, but also it isn\u2019t just instant death of a sorcerer summons five of them and tells them to kill Mnemon or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T14:52:37-08:00","id":1292861,"title":"","content":".... Wait. Maybe I got this wrong, but don't the rules in Exalted modern make it so that even heroic mortals can parry bullets?<br /> <br /> I thought this is deadly for mortal formations and infrastructure. And a hassle for combat specced Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T15:28:13-08:00","id":1292867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292731#post1292731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If &quot;heredity&quot; is a thing, any given people that managed to exist mostly uniformly will form a mostly uniform ethnicity. This is especially true of people with geographic barriers, like the whole of Creation.<br /> And heredity is a thing in Creation.<br /> So most populaces will be relatively uniform. And being surprised or wary of something different, or assuming better off the similar, will happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but this is kind of why a demon that stokes racial tension may not work well though.<br /> If most villages and settlements are pretty uniform in terms of ethnic markers, there's no ethnic minority for the demon to look like.*<br /> <br /> *Actually, you often will get different ethnicities in close contact, but in linguistic-cultural terms, not &quot;racial&quot; terms. Like French and Breton, or Castilian and Galician, or Gujerati and Punjabi. So there's no racially distinct characteristics for the demon to copy.<br /> <br /> A more successful way to differentiate between ethnic groups would be accent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-28-2019, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T15:53:26-08:00","id":1292870,"title":"","content":"mhmm. I agree. Sowing dissent on this basis alone doesn't work very well, nor does it make for an interesting creature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T16:03:41-08:00","id":1292874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292861#post1292861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.... Wait. Maybe I got this wrong, but don't the rules in Exalted modern make it so that even heroic mortals can parry bullets?<br /> <br /> I thought this is deadly for mortal formations and infrastructure. And a hassle for combat specced Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being attacked from miles away tends to be a surprise attack.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T16:42:38-08:00","id":1292881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292874#post1292874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being attacked from miles away tends to be a surprise attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also really hard for even most Exalts to really retaliate against.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T17:00:29-08:00","id":1292883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292731#post1292731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The steps for that to become what we usually understand as racism are short and natural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, they're something generated by particular circumstances and political considerations, and the assertion that they're natural and inevitable arises from self-fulfilling propaganda that functions to deflect people away from considering the underlying basis of personal and systemic biases.<br /> <br /> I recently learned interesting things about the history of American racial profiles of peoples from Southeast Asia, emerging as they did from both immigration policies that were skewed towards permitting the entry of trained professionals (hence the &quot;smart Asians&quot; thing) to try and create a counternarrative to Soviet propaganda calling out American racism, while also incorporating that profile into propaganda concerned with reinforcing systemic oppression of black Americans, by comparing them unfavourably to so-called &quot;model minorities&quot; to promote an idea in which poverty in black communities could be ascribed to an inherent laziness (and implicit intellectual inferiority)&quot;. This also corresponding to a time when the dwindling Republican party started deliberately targeting Southern racists as an untapped source of votes.<br /> <br /> <i>That</i> also being the time when traditionally marginalized people such as those of Irish and Italian descent got to be upgraded to the same status of &quot;white&quot; as the previously generally more powerful English, German and Dutch-Americans, since they also could be marshalled into that system.<br /> <br /> Plus things about how European ideas about some inherent inferiority of African people largely came a good deal of time after several major economies became heavily invested in slave labour, with the original basis of the African slave market owing a lot to its proximity to a growing economy in the Arab world that had a demand for it. A lot of those ideas tended to be framed directly in circumstances of justifying slavery.<br /> <br /> The Arab world that has incidentally often been home to a variety of peoples of many ethnic backgrounds and phenotypes, who if not living harmoniously, still didn't really have the kinds of racial divisions that a lot of us would be familiar with.<br /> <br /> Plus the matter of how a lot of European national identities owe a lot to official programs to centralize power and homogenize the social makeup to allow for more standardized models of government.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T18:59:59-08:00","id":1292904,"title":"","content":"Fine then. One shot hit. Transforms into a missile in a bright flash of light that is obvious to the target.<br /> <br /> Extra damage to manses or buildings or people. <br /> <br /> Wow. I need more breeds of Predator Drones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T20:30:54-08:00","id":1292925,"title":"","content":"Mind, considering how a number of ethnic tensions in post-colonial societies can trace their roots back to the manner in which colonial powers deliberately cultivated divisions and conflicts between those groups, creating enduring legacies that exploded violently when colonialism was no longer valid... the idea of a breed of saboteur demon with the intrinsic function of fostering and enflaming such divisions would not be out of place, when understood in terms of creating those divisions in service of an agenda, rather than harnessing something that is already intrinsically present, or just a stone's throw away.<br /> <br /> It would even be able to serve a natural function in its own society, as fostering division and hatred between different varieties of demon seems like a natural quality of the environment of Hell, serving Cecylene's role and inclinations as an enforcer of Hell's hierarchy in particular, and the general distrust, paranoia and spite of Yozis in particular. I would imagine that the bulk of such work ultimately falls to a lot of governing Second Circle Demons, and the occasional select Third Circle, following directives passed down from on high, but could see a particular kind of demon emerging from one of Cecylene's souls to help perpetuate it at the root level. Maybe they'd be born from Lucien.<br /> <br /> Such creatures would probably be a bit more limited in Creation, and need to adjust their ideas if ever in situations where they're not dealing with a society promoting divisive policies, but they could make a game attempt at it. Enough to cause damage that would attract some power to root them out, and leave a few scars that persist past their removal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T03:31:37-08:00","id":1292976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292883#post1292883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively,[...]interesting lore</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't see how any of that alternates off my statement. Large centralized powers playing at whatever they can to remain large centralized powers is pretty normal.<br /> <br /> I missed one thing in my statement, though: Friction and normalization.<br /> Friction helps turn wariness into mistrust. Normalization gives an idea more inertia (be it towards more prejudice or less). With neither things should pacify themselves over time.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is veering off helping the op.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T03:49:23-08:00","id":1292979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1292976#post1292976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't see how any of that alternates off my statement. Large centralized powers playing at whatever they can to remain large centralized powers is pretty normal.<br /> <br /> I missed one thing in my statement, though: Friction and normalization.<br /> Friction helps turn wariness into mistrust. Normalization gives an idea more inertia (be it towards more prejudice or less). With neither things should pacify themselves over time.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is veering off helping the op.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no. This is all very interesting. Keep talking, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-02T00:44:44-08:00","id":1293254,"title":"","content":"Just checked out scroll of Kings. Should I just put the stats of the predator drone like a gigantic steam cannon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T04:06:53-08:00","id":1295009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1291770#post1291770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two attacks? One suicide launch, another one that lets it carry out harassment? I'm thinking of a massive metamorphosis into a missile for the first, and mouths that spit out death threats for the second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could work, depends how effective the secondary attack is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T04:09:34-08:00","id":1295010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1295009#post1295009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could work, depends how effective the secondary attack is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.. machine gun stats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T19:48:59-08:00","id":1295189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1295010#post1295010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh.. machine gun stats?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't exactly call a machine gun a tool of &quot;harassment.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-08T20:35:34-08:00","id":1295203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291469-potentially-politically-problematic-homebrew?p=1295189#post1295189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't exactly call a machine gun a tool of &quot;harassment.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>To be frank, I was more thinking on 'I need a weapon that would pin down an enemy'. It can't be too powerful. That's what the sacrificial main weapon is for. So I chose machine gun. Its meant to harass, capable of doing damage, but its also a bad idea to depend on it to fight your battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-09T20:41:16-08:00","id":1295465,"title":"","content":"What edition are you homebrewing for? I assumed 3rd ed, but you're referencing a lot of 2nd ed material. I'm familiar with both, just wondering. <br /> <br /> To continue the discussion re: genesis of racism. Fear of the &quot;Other&quot; is a pretty common human drive, but most specific examples of racial tension or conflict have their roots in structural factors like the ones Isator Levi mentioned. It's usually a convenient excuse for fulfilling some other need or want, rather than the driving factor. <br /> <br /> If you need cheap labour, designate a nearby people as inferior and enslave them. If you need resources or land, demonise the people who have what you want and take it. If you need someone to blame for the fallout of your economic policies, blame immigrants so you can hold onto power. Fear of the other doesn't create societal conflict on its own (though it can give rise to individual violence). There's usually some individual or faction with something to gain by tapping into and directing that impulse at a target, wherever you see widespread racial violence erupt. <br /> <br /> Now if your demon works by making one culture seem like the aggressor by carrying out violence and sabotage, people might get fearful enough to strike back in order to deal with a perceived threat. But physical racial traits aren't always going to be the best way to do that. Just look at the way the Irish were treated by other whites not too long ago. People's understanding of race is fluid and malleable, and cultural signifiers can mean as much as your skin tone or the shape of your nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}